      "message": "Yes, std::move does not make guarantees, but specific implementations of functions which take an r value reference do make guarantees. I wonder if it was passing because when we call `AccessorProviderEntry(std::move(provider))`, the AccessorProviderEntry constructor implementation calls `mProvider(provider)` instead of `mProvider(std::move(provider))`. Since the r value reference is copied instead of moved now it makes a copy, but if it is moved, it will call the constructor std::shared_ptr\u003cT\u003e(T\u0026\u0026), which guarantees to clear the r value reference.",
